# graphlaw seed policy graph — SHACL shapes over the act: transition-proposal
# vocabulary (lane P1, operator FOND decomposition, v26.10.22).
#
# A Claude Code PreToolUse hook converts each file-tool call into a one-node
# RDF transition proposal:
#
#   [] a act:ToolCall ; act:tool "Edit" ; act:targetsFile "<abs path>" .
#
# and asks the compiled graphlaw wasm module (driven by graphlaw-run over
# packet-4 stdio) to validate the proposal against THESE shapes via the
# `shacl` ABI op. `conforms: false` => refuse before any disk alteration.
#
# Each rule is a separately-named sh:NodeShape with one sh:not over a compound
# node shape, so a violation names its rule IRI (typed refusal, per the repo
# convention) instead of a generic NotConstraintComponent on one blob shape.
#
# SCOPE (honest): this seed graph encodes exactly THREE rules — the three
# witnessed guards' rules — as a starting corpus. It is NOT the full kh:
# refusal-hook pattern and does not cover Bash escape hatches, caller
# identity/lease standing, or per-lane authority. Sequenced increments:
# docs/jira/v26.10.22/designs/graphlaw-admission-blueprint.md

@prefix act:  <http://graphlaw.org/act#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

### RULE 1 — coordinator-owned manifests (GL-SEED-R1)
### Mirrors .claude/hooks/manifest_guard.py: lane file tools never touch the
### root Cargo.toml / deny.toml; the coordinator applies manifest transitions
### via Bash (scripted edit) — that path is the deliberate escape hatch.
<http://graphlaw.org/policy/seed#R1ManifestCoordinatorOwned>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass act:ToolCall ;
    sh:not [
        a sh:NodeShape ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:targetsFile ;
            sh:pattern "(^|/)(Cargo\\.toml|deny\\.toml)$" ;
        ] ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:tool ;
            sh:in ( "Edit" "Write" "MultiEdit" "NotebookEdit" ) ;
        ] ;
    ] .

### RULE 2 — wasm pin immutability (GL-SEED-R2)
### priv/graphlaw.wasm is a pinned artifact; its digest is re-pinned by the
### registry flow, never by a lane file-tool edit. Scoped to Edit per the
### witnessed guard class.
<http://graphlaw.org/policy/seed#R2WasmPinImmutable>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass act:ToolCall ;
    sh:not [
        a sh:NodeShape ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:targetsFile ;
            sh:pattern "(^|/)priv/graphlaw\\.wasm$" ;
        ] ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:tool ;
            sh:hasValue "Edit" ;
        ] ;
    ] .

### RULE 3 — receipt surface is generated (GL-SEED-R3)
### registry/ projections and ARTIFACTS.blake3 are regenerated by the registry
### sync flow, never hand-edited.
<http://graphlaw.org/policy/seed#R3ReceiptSurfaceGenerated>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass act:ToolCall ;
    sh:not [
        a sh:NodeShape ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:targetsFile ;
            sh:pattern "(^|/)registry/[^/]+\\.(json|ttl)$|(^|/)registry/ARTIFACTS\\.blake3$" ;
        ] ;
        sh:property [
            sh:path act:tool ;
            sh:in ( "Edit" "Write" "MultiEdit" "NotebookEdit" ) ;
        ] ;
    ] .
